WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:06.270
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, Walking Dead
is coming back in 4 weeks and just to get

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:14.180
us all pumped up and ready I’m doing a weekly
countdown series of bonus videos for the characters

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:23.599
and some of my own personal favorites from
the last couple of seasons.

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:29.169
This one will be all about Rick.

00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:33.120
Hello any new people, if you’re just finding
me I’m going to be doing weekly walking

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.750
dead videos and a weekly giveaway.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.330
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.640
I’ll be doing a Q&amp;A tomorrow where I’ll
announce this week’s winner.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.960
More details about all that at the end of
this.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.330
I know farmer Rick got a lot of hate for what
went down at the prison in season 4 and all

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.420
the chaos in the aftermath but that Rick is
dead.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.340
Long Live Farmer Rick.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:03.360
Just to get things started, here’s my top
5 Rick Moments from the show so far.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.600
Careful for spoilers from everything on the
show through Season 4.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.929
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go

00:01:09.929 --> 00:01:12.710
Number 5 - Rick Kills Shane

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.789
Bonus points for Carl killing Walker Shane,
so Shane was killed twice in rapid succession.

00:01:15.789 --> 00:01:18.840
I love that they give the bigger characters
epic deaths.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.119
And they made it a family affair.

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:26.819
Both times Shane was put down were self defense,
Rick with the Knife and Carl with the gun.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:39.210
This is one of the better examples of Rick
finding it in himself to kill one of his former

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.210
best friends.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.740
Let that be a reminder to Professor Mullett,
Eugene or even Bob if he thinks about hitting

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.740
the bottle while they’re still trying to
escape Terminus.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.740
I feel like Rick’s final battle with the
Governor during season 4 was just as personal,

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:46.740
but he and Shane shared so much between the
two of them.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.270
They were essentially this warped messed up
family unit with Two dads and one mom.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:54.639
Shane had been headed down hill all season,
so by the time Rick took him out I felt almost

00:01:54.639 --> 00:01:55.639
no sympathy for him.

00:01:55.639 --> 00:01:58.509
Although, do you remember back in the second
half of season 4 when Rick and Carl break

00:01:58.509 --> 00:01:59.509
into that house.

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:01.990
Carl breaks down and throws Shane in Rick’s
face.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.779
They said, behind the scenes, the actors were
thinking of the most messed up terrible thing

00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:09.550
Carl could say to Rick, just to get him to
react.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.290
And they came up with Shane.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.650
Number 4 - Rick Kills Dave’s Gang in Season
2

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.409
It was episode 9, the mid season premiere.

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:22.650
This is a classic example of quick tempered
Rick shooting first and asking questions later.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.269
He and Herschel were at Hatlin’s bar talking
about Herschel’s dead wife and being guilty

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:29.129
about how he’d led Maggie and Beth on about
her condition.

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:35.170
Cut to random appearance by Michael Raymond
James from Terriers and Tony who were part

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.709
of a large group of nomads.

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:41.590
They press Rick and Herschel about the location
of the farm so they can bring the group but

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:44.750
push comes to shove and Rick just ain’t
havin’ it.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:49.700
He finishes Dave off with a headshot, but
Tony who’s huge takes three bullets before

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.000
he goes down.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.150
I feel like everytime the show does a bar
scene, something terrible happens.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.189
So anytime a new one shows up I’ve always
thought it’s the director reminding us visually

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:03.370
that this is like the opposite of cheers.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.299
You will never be glad you came.

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:15.110
Number 3 - Rick Hacks of Herschel’s Leg

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.110
This was from the season 3 premiere and that
leg did not go quickly.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.129
It was really messy and really awesome at
the same time.

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:26.620
Herschel makes the mistake of assuming a body
lying on the floor is completely dead but

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:30.790
it reanimates, bites him and Rick performs
surgery right there on the spot.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.970
The hack job was something right out of a
b-horror movie, which was probably just as

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:40.610
much fun for the props team to set up as it
was for us to watch it unfold on tv.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:50.129
But after it’s all done, everyone looks
up from the mess and sees all a new group

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:57.409
of survivors walk up with WTF faces like what
just happened here.

00:03:57.409 --> 00:04:03.400
I think a lot of the season 4 complaints people
had during the time at the prison were mostly

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:09.689
that it felt like a long slow rot compared
to the crazy intensity of moments like this.

00:04:09.689 --> 00:04:13.819
It’s always interesting to hear Scott Gimple
and the other cast members talk about changes

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:17.209
to the tone of the show from half season to
half season.

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:27.970
Thematically every 8 episodes, they completely
change what the show is.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:31.979
Number 2 - Rick Clears The Prison Like a Video
Game

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:34.920
This was also from that same first episode
in season 3.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.970
The survivors had the task of clearing the
prison for habitation.

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:41.199
And it just turns into this video game killing
spree.

00:04:41.199 --> 00:04:47.030
Like Rick is just chopping meat in a barrel.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:53.979
This is what I’m hoping to see again in
Season 5.

00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:56.020
maybe even the first episode.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:04.330
It would be a nice callback to them clearing
the prison.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:09.870
Only instead of clearing Terminus so they
can live there, they clear it so they can

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.020
escape.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:16.699
Some of the cooler takedowns are when they
start finding the armored guard walkers.

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:23.030
Armor that Glenn then later used to escape
in season 4.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:27.090
Number 1 - Rick Bites out Joe’s Neck

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.720
This is the best example of crazy Rick.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:34.440
The I don’t give a crap about anything but
making this threat in front of me go away.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.770
It was one of the crazier scenes from the
comic book, usually the show is totally different,

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:45.639
but it does do some of the bigger stuff from
the comic.

00:05:45.639 --> 00:05:51.229
It was like Rick shook off whatever funk had
been on him the whole season and roared back

00:05:51.229 --> 00:05:56.830
to life all over Joe’s neck.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:02.139
They said that when they filmed the scene,
Greg Nicotero came up to Andrew Lincoln and

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:03.610
said Chicken or Fish.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:07.740
And Andrew Lincoln took a sec till it was
explained the chunk of neck he’d be biting

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.099
out would be uncooked meat.

00:06:10.099 --> 00:06:16.280
He chose the chicken.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:21.190
And he said the actor playing Joe just told
him to really lay into it.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.190
Like go crazy.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.360
The whole thing was surreal.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:28.810
And that next morning when he and Daryl are
sitting there in the mess of the dead claimers.

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.570
Rick seems totally over it.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.560
Like he’s already moved on.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:38.900
I’ve been calling him Machine Gun Rick when
I refer to season 5 stuff, but really we should

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.300
just call him Crazy Rick.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.699
Like stab you in a dirty alleyway Rick.

00:06:42.699 --> 00:06:45.860
If any of you really didn’t like season
4 in general, I think a lot of your prayers

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.389
for more action have been answered with this
first half of season 5.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:52.610
I’ve been following the production as they
shoot the second half of season 5, so just

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:59.610
turn the volume down till this tag goes away
if you don’t want to know what’s going

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:00.610
on...okay.

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:04.050
So it seems like the second half of season
5 is going to be spent on the run.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.050
The survivors that is.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:10.569
I still haven’t seen beth and it seems like
they continued to shoot at that creepy hospital

00:07:10.569 --> 00:07:15.690
we saw her at in the trailer.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.030
okay spoilers over.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:22.849
I don’t want to use the term Hunters, just
because that’s a whole group in the comics,

00:07:22.849 --> 00:07:30.720
but Rick is much more of a predator running
point for the survivors.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:36.410
I can’t show it here in this video but during
comic con they aired a gag reel of Andrew

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:40.720
Lincoln warming up for scenes by screaming
obscenities running around punching stuff

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.639
like he was warming up for a boxing match.

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:45.410
That’s the kind of Rick I’m really excited
to see this year.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.500
Once the episodes start we can talk more about
character arcs, but for the first couple of

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.870
episodes it’s going to be all claws and
teeth.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.610
Here’s a big question for you guys.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:54.220
What’s you favorite badass Rick Grimes moment
from the show.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.889
If you’ve read the comics it’s okay to
comment on something from that but please

00:07:56.889 --> 00:07:58.289
use spoiler tags.

